---
/**
 * Product (marketing-site story 3, CAP-2): how Wipestation is designed to
 * work, from the bench to the job, the certificate and its verification, the
 * destroy path, fleet and integration, and licensing. Every claim is wrapped
 * in its `<Capability>`; metadata carries no guarded phrase.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Capability from "../components/Capability.astro";
import { body, grid, h1, h2, h3, item, link, notice, prose, secondaryLink, section } from "../lib/ui";
---

<Base
  title="How the product is designed to work"
  description="Wipestation from the bench to the job, the certificate and its verification, with the destroy path, fleet, integration and licensing. Every capability carries its status."
>
  <p class={notice}>
    Pre-launch: every pre-release build runs against simulated drives.
  </p>
  <h1 class:list={[h1, "mt-3"]}>How the product is designed to work</h1>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>
      Wipestation is one program with a desktop interface for the operator at the bench and an
      HTTP API for everything else. Each step below is what it is designed to do, labelled with
      where it stands today; the <a href="/capabilities/" class={link}>capabilities page</a> lists
      them all.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class={section} aria-labelledby="bench">
    <h2 id="bench" class={h2}>From bench to certificate</h2>
    <ol class={grid}>
      <Capability id="drive-sanitization" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>1. The bench and the method</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so the operator loads an asset into a bay on a map of the real bench, and sanitize SSDs and HDDs to NIST Clear or Purge, with the method selected
          from the asset's intent and classification.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="nvme-sanitize" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>2. Honest NVMe Sanitize</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed to issue NVMe Sanitize first (crypto erase on self-encrypting drives, block
          erase otherwise) with an explicit fallback order, never a quiet overwrite.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="hpa-dco-clear" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>3. Hidden regions first</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed to detect and clear HPA and DCO hidden regions before Purge, and to refuse to
          report Purge if they were not reached.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="outcome-bearing-job" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>4. One job per asset</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so every attempt on an asset, retries and verification included, composes into
          one signed certificate per asset rather than separate records to reconcile later.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="command-level-evidence" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>5. Command-level evidence</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          The certificate is designed to record each issued opcode, its return status and the log
          pages read, so an auditor sees proof, not prose.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="offline-verification" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>6. Offline-verifiable</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so an Ed25519 signature over canonical JSON lets anyone with the public key
          check a certificate without contacting the vendor.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ol>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="open-cert-format" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Open certificate format</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          The JSON-LD certificate schema is to be published, so third parties can build their own
          verifiers.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="verification-portal" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Customer-facing verification portal</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          A planned branded link an ITAD can hand its own customer. An index, never the authority:
          the certificate stays checkable with the public key alone.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class={section} aria-labelledby="destroy">
    <h2 id="destroy" class={h2}>When an asset cannot be reused</h2>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="destruction-attestation" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>The destroy path</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so that if an asset is physically destroyed, for example shredded after erasure
          failed, the operator attests the destruction, optionally with a second person's concurrence, and it
          joins the same chain of custody.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="validate-workflow" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Programmatic Validate workflow</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          A planned registry for the NIST Rev. 2 Validate step, per media class, kept separate
          from the verification run after each erasure.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class={section} aria-labelledby="fleet">
    <h2 id="fleet" class={h2}>Fleet and integration</h2>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="fleet-coordination" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>LAN fleet coordination</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so stations on one network find each other by mDNS and agree on a lead by
          deterministic lead election, with no server to install.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="air-gap-operation" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Air-gapped by design</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so an air-gapped station keeps full product value with no connection to the
          vendor, ever.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="erp-integration" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>ERP integration</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed for REST in and out, webhooks on job changes and certificate signing, and
          asset-id lookups, so the ERP stays the system of record.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="itam-integration" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>ITAM and service-desk integration</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Planned links from each job to the asset record in an ITAM and the ticket in a service
          desk such as ServiceNow or Jira.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class={section} aria-labelledby="licensing">
    <h2 id="licensing" class={h2}>Licensing</h2>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="per-success-licensing" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Per-success licensing</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          A licence credit is designed to be spent only on a verified Clear or Purge success;
          failures, aborts and re-runs are free.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="licence-decides-at-start" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Licensing decides at the start, never mid-erasure.</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          A station checks its licence before each job starts. A job that started covered is always
          certified, however long it runs, and a station with a valid licence never needs a network
          connection to keep working.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-slate-700">
      <a href="/pricing/" class={secondaryLink}>How pricing works before launch</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 rounded border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4" aria-labelledby="join">
    <h2 id="join" class={h2}>Try it early</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-slate-700">
      Early access means pre-release builds against simulated drives, and a say in what ships
      first.
      <a href="/early-access/" class={secondaryLink}>How early access works</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
